# Autosave and Continue. The harness keeps saves in memory (never in the config directory), so every script starts with none.
# Layout (1400x800): main menu without a save: Versus (150,250), Load game (150,310); with an autosave Continue is the top item:
#   Continue (150,220), Versus (150,280), Load game (150,340). Standard row (905,224); Play (808,712); Back on the mode list
#   (700,712); in game Back (125,25); Submit (841,90).
wait 20
capture continue-none      # no save yet: the menu has no Continue
click 150 250        # Versus
wait 30
click 905 224        # Standard
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
clicksq 0 0 e2
wait 40
clicksq 0 0 e4
wait 40
click 841 90         # Submit: the autosave is written
wait 90
click 125 25         # Back to the mode list
wait 30
click 700 712        # Back to the main menu
wait 40
capture continue-menu
click 150 220        # Continue
wait 120
capture continue-resumed   # same game: Black to move, Turn 1, e4 played
clicksq 0 1 e7       # a move that is never submitted
wait 60
clicksq 0 1 e5
wait 60
click 125 25         # Back (the unsubmitted move is not saved)
wait 30
click 700 712
wait 40
click 150 220        # Continue again
wait 120
capture continue-pending-dropped   # Black to move with the e7 pawn back on e7
